			"date": "2024-09-27T14:00:03.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> It all starts from realizing they're not something you can \"work around\", they're a thing you \"work with\" (like events, or promises, or &lt;select&gt; elements) and if you're not or can't then it could be says that your abstraction might just be wrong...</p><p>Just sayin. 😏</p>",
